    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded in 973 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#tailapa-ii">Tailapa II</a>, who overthrew the Rashtrakutas and claimed descent from the Chalukyas of Badami.</li><li>Its kings ruled from Kalyani and fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#chola-empire">Chola Empire</a> for two centuries over the Raichur doab and Vengi.</li><li>Its courts produced the Mitakshara, rich Kannada literature and an ornate temple style that inspired the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#hoysala-empire">Hoysalas</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Someshvara I, stricken by incurable illness in 1068, ended his life by drowning in the Tungabhadra river, a death recorded by the poet Bilhana and in inscriptions.</p></aside>
    </section>

